From 10209de65d2accda1d7cdb8e178f41f9a20f166f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 05:42:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] aegisos: disable credential_capture flag, revert to inert
 pending redesign

This is a deliberate safety revert of an owner-approved decision, not a
mistake being undone. Once 0002/0003 (kept, unchanged) made this flag's
release-config placement and permission genuinely correct and the flag
became active for the first time on real hardware, re-verification found
a confirmed security regression: an ordinary (non-decoy) am switch-user
to a PIN-protected secondary user landed on a fully unlocked desktop with
zero credential check performed (no LockSettingsService 'Verifying
primary lockscreen credential' logcat line at all for that switch). The
mechanism also did not achieve its original goal - the decoy double-PIN
UX bug it was meant to fix persists via a different code path
(dismissKeyguardThenExecute / PrimaryBouncerInteractor re-showing the
bouncer). See .superpowers/sdd/task-2-fix-report.md for the full evidence.

Setting state: DISABLED here makes android.multiuser.Flags.credentialCapture()
false again, which keeps UserController.setInitialConfig() from ever
consulting frameworks/base's config_multiuserSkipKeyguardWhenSwitchingToUnlockedUsers
resource override (0018) - the guard at UserController.java around line 542
means that resource flip is inert on its own whenever this flag is off, so
it does not need to be reverted separately.

How to actually fix the original double-PIN UX bug without reintroducing a
device-wide keyguard bypass is left as a future redesign problem, not
solved reactively here.

Keeps: 0002 (correct aconfig/cp2a/ directory placement) and 0003 (READ_ONLY
permission for cp2a's RELEASE_ACONFIG_REQUIRE_ALL_READ_ONLY policy) - both
are genuine, correct fixes independent of whether the flag is enabled or
disabled.
---
 .../android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto  | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto b/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto
index f18ae512b..2af5b42d9 100644
--- a/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto
+++ b/aconfig/cp2a/android.multiuser/credential_capture_flag_values.textproto
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 flag_value {
   package: "android.multiuser"
   name: "credential_capture"
-  state: ENABLED
+  state: DISABLED
   permission: READ_ONLY
 }
